# Certificate material never belongs in source control, even though the root .gitignore already
# excludes these patterns repo-wide - this is a deliberate belt-and-suspenders reminder right where
# people will actually drop files.
*.pfx
*.p12
*.pem
*.key
*.cer
*.crt

# Also exclude plain-text password/notes files people drop next to a cert (e.g. "password.txt") -
# this app never reads a password from a file, but nothing stops someone from leaving one here, and
# it must never end up committed. This folder isn't used for anything else, so *.txt is safe to
# blanket-exclude aside from the explicit README allowlisted below.
*.txt

!.gitignore
!README.md
